  "full_text": "It's like, okay. There's a house in New Orleans. They call the rising sun. And it's been the ruin of a poor boy in God. My mother was a tailor. She sewed my blue jeans. My father was a gambling man. New Orleans. Only thing a gambler needs is a suitcase and a trunk. And the only time that he's satisfied is when he's on and drunk. Tell your children not to do what I have done. Sin and misery in the house of the rising sun. Well, I got one foot on the platform. The other on the train. I'm going back to New Orleans to wear the bowling in New Orleans.",
